bring-up plan, first steps, for Board T (fictional):
  1. connect the debug UART (debug connector J7); see the first boot messages
  2. practise recovery (usb) before writing to on-board storage
  3. boot the known-good image; save its devicetree and kernel log as the reference
  4. read the devicetree: memory, CPUs, interrupt controller, timer, UART, clocks, resets, pins
  5. bring up in order: MMU, interrupts, timer, UART, GPIO heartbeat, storage, then the rest
  documents to collect: TRM (full), errata (yes), board schematic, the vendor's devicetree source
